# Registers on the session's copy history (doc/design/registers.md): what
# other panes copied ("copy:" records it before the keys, as a terminal's
# visual mode would), and the client's clipboard ("clipboard:").

=== a terminal's lines put with p
text:
|one
two
copy: line from the terminal
keys: p
want:
one
|from the terminal
two

=== a terminal's copy is the newest yank, "0
text:
|ab
copy: char T
keys: x"0p
want:
b|T

=== deletes of lines shift through "1 and "2
text:
|one
two
three
keys: dddd"2p
want:
three
|one

=== a delete within a line goes to "-
text:
|ab cd
next
keys: dwjdd"-P
want:
ab| cd

=== "+p puts the client's clipboard
text:
|x
clipboard: from outside
keys: "+p
want:
xfrom outsid|e

=== the clipboard's text ending with a line break goes in as lines
text:
|x
clipboard: line\n
keys: "+p
want:
x
|line

=== a clipboard put repeats with .
text:
|x
clipboard: ab
keys: "+p.
want:
xaba|b

=== a clipboard that cannot be read is an error
text:
|x
keys: "+p
want:
|x
error: yes
